.SH NAME
.PP
auto-ldap-client-setup - Configure authentication via LDAP

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-ldap-client-setup URI OU O cacert
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
URI     - URI of the LDAP server
OU      - Organizational unit (e.g. people)
O       - Organization
cacert  - cert file
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-ldap-client-setup
command configures the system to authenticate users via a
remote LDAP server.  It installs ldap software if necessary,
and modifies the necessary configuration files to work with
the LDAP server information provided on the command-line.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-ldap-client-setup ldap://ldap.my.domain people my.domain ./cacert.crt
.ad
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO

ldap(3), ldap.conf(5)

